  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 250 PM EDT Monday...\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Seasonable temperatures and dry this week.\n\nAfternoon analysis shows low pressure moving out to sea as high \npressure over the Midwest builds into the region. Clouds have been \nmuch slower to clear than previously expected across the SE half of \nthe area this afternoon. Limited insolation has impacted afternoon \nhigh temperatures quite a bit with Louisa and Farmville currently in \nthe upper 70s while areas near and SE of Richmond remain in the \nupper 60s to low 70s. A limited window for additional heating is \npossible but most of the area will fall short of the mid 70s. \n\nA dry cold front is starting to make southward progress this \nafternoon with winds turning to the NW as much drier air filters \ninto the area. Winds will generally be light tonight inland but will \nbecome breezy near the coast as the cooler/drier air interacts with \nthe warm local waters. Low temps fall into the mid to upper 40s \ninland but linger in the low 50s near the coast and into NE NC. \nCooler than average temps continue on Tuesday with highs in the 60s \nto low 70s despite full (or nearly full) sunshine. Light winds and \nclear skies will lead to the coolest night of the season (so far) \nwith low temps mainly in the low to mid 40s for most of the area \nTuesday night. \n\nRemaining dry as high pressure moves offshore Wednesday into \nThursday with warmer temperatures returning to the region. Highs for \ninland areas rebound into the mid 70s on Wednesday (low 70s near the \ncoast) with upper 70s and low 80s forecast on Thursday. Another dry \nfront is forecast to cross the region late Thursday.  \n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Moisture does not return until late this weekend \ninto early next week.\n\nBy late this weekend into early next week, there is increasing \npotential for moisture to be pulled northward from the western Gulf \nand then pushed eastward across the region ahead of a trough over \nthe mid-Mississippi Valley. Confidence remains low with regard to \ndetails. However, global ensemble guidance does show PW values \nrising above normal, with some deeper moisture in the 700-300mb \nlayer. Given this, a chc for showers returns to the forecast Sunday \nand Monday. Temperatures should remain near average late this \nweekend and early next week.",
